# 16 Subroutine calls that return captures: (?&name(<group>,...))
# https://www.pcre.org/current/doc/html/pcre2pattern.html
#
# Needs PCRE2 10.47 or newer. PHP bundles 10.44, where the call-argument
# syntax is a compile error ("syntax error in subpattern name").
#
# What it is: normally a subroutine call like (?1) or (?&name) runs a
# group's sub-pattern and then discards whatever that run captured. Since
# 10.47 a call can list capture groups to RETURN to the calling context,
# written (?1(GROUP,...)) or (?&name(<group>,...)). After the call those
# groups hold what the subroutine matched, visible to backreferences and
# $matches.
#
# What it enables: (?(DEFINE)...) rule libraries that also export what
# they captured. A "date rule" defined once can hand its year back to
# every call site.

# Expect: 0: a=b
#         1: <unset>
#         2: a
# The DEFINEd rule "pair" is invoked by call and the call returns group
# <x> ("a") to the caller. Group 2 is set AFTER the call. Without the
# (<x>) argument it would be <unset>.
/(?(DEFINE)(?<pair>(?<x>\w)=(?<y>\w)))(?&pair(<x>))/
    a=b

# Expect: 0: Saturday,Sat
#         1: <unset>
#         2: Sat
# A backreference consumes a capture made INSIDE the finished call.
# \k<short> matches "Sat" because the call exported <short>.
/(?(DEFINE)(?<wd>(?|(?<short>Sat)urday|(?<short>Sun)day)))(?&wd(<short>)),\k<short>/
    Saturday,Sat
